 alien DNA out in the world right  now spread by somebody who encountered  it many years ago part of the film's  effectiveness comes from the fact that  it leaves those questions unanswered and  dials up the paranoia over just what the  thing is and what it can do but what we  do know is that it can infiltrate  mankind  assimilate seamlessly if it wants to -  who's to say it hasn't already as the  paranoia over who might be infected by  the thing sets in the men of the station  quickly begin to turn on each other  this conflict it's a fever pitch when  nulls tries to leave McCready out in the  storm after finding his torn jacket  outside which suggests that he may have  been attacked at some point child what  if we wrong about him wrong McCready  eventually makes his way back inside and  ultimately takes command of the  survivors but this seemingly vital plot  point is quickly forgotten  is there a logical reason for it to have  been there is it really proof that Mack  was already assimilated and that the  organisms controlling him are just  really good at hiding it or is something  else going on the film never answers  that question but it does feed into the  famous final scene in a major way  the film's iconic blood test sequence  raises another interesting question  about the nature of the thing Palmer is  the one who turns out to be infected and  we see his blood basically jump out of  its petri dish when confronted with a  hot wire we also know that the thing  will divide into different parts that  will act independently if they need to  and that it can infect people on a  microbiotic level does all of this mean  that infected blood get in some way act  or at least survive on its own there's  no short supply of blood scattered  throughout the film both in the  Norwegian station and among the  Americans if it's somehow able to retain  the alien organism within it it could at  the very least survive out in the cold  if it's able to transfer itself to other  tissue it comes into contact with it  could do even more than that fire can  destroy most things but it can't  eliminate every last drop of blood the  thing's ending is famously ambiguous  after destroying the station MacCready  stumbles outside with a bottle of scotch  in hand to find child's returning  claiming his absence from the final  struggle was because he had left to look  for Blair  worried about me we've got any surprises  for each other I don't think we're much  shape do anything this moment has led to  a number of fan theories hypothesizing  which of two men might be infected it  could be either Mac or child's or even  both not only just  wait here for a little while  see what happens some fans claim max  bottle isn't filled with scotch  but gasoline and that he tricked childs  into proving he isn't human by making  him drink it others believe that his  little smile at the end could mean that  Mac is the thing the closest thing to a  definitive answer may have come from  cinematographer Dean Cundy who said he  and carpenter used eye light earlier in  the film to suggest who was human and  who wasn't if you look closely that  could very well mean it's likely the  thing is living in child's whether it's  child's or Macready there is a strong  implication at the end of the film that  at least one of the two men remains  infected by the thing which suggests  that the alien story is far from over  so what happens now if only one of them  is the thing it's quite likely it will  eventually assimilate the other human  body could the thing then hold out long  enough to wait for help could they feign  death and eventually assimilate other  healthier humans could they even let the  ice reclaim them and return to the same  kind of stasis from which the thing  apparently came whatever the case may be  this story clearly doesn't end with  child's and McCready and the version of  Earth the film depicts could well be  doomed check out one of our newest  videos right here pl